{
  "id": "PSI-159",
  "summary_plain": "This investigation burned gaseous fuels like ethane, propane, and butane using spherical burners on the International Space Station to study cool diffusion flames. Understanding how cool flames behave helps researchers improve fuel efficiency in engines and advance fire safety in space. By examining these low-temperature flames in microgravity, scientists can better predict and prevent unexpected combustion behaviors.",
  "summary_expert": "The Advanced Combustion via Microgravity Experiments / Cool Flames Investigation with Gases (ACME CFI-G) conducted 333 tests aboard the International Space Station utilizing the Combustion Integrated Rack. The investigation varied fuel types (including ethane, propane, and n-butane), oxygen mole fractions ranging from 0.18 to 0.40, and ambient pressures from 50 to 331 kPa, across normal and inverse spherical burner configurations. Recorded outcomes across the test matrix included hot ignition with self-extinguishment in 175 tests, flow termination after hot ignition in 88 tests, no hot ignition in 61 tests, flash with self-extinguishment in 8 tests, and no hot ignition with flow terminated in 1 test, with burn times spanning 0 to 304 seconds. Primary operational challenges included controlling ignition energy to directly initiate cool flames and discerning cool flame presence, which was complicated by catalyst-induced reignition from exposed platinum type-B thermocouples.",
  "key_findings": [
    {
      "text": "A total of 280 hot flames were ignited or naturally reignited during the CFI-G experiment across Increments 64-66, with 33, 225, and 22 flames ignited in the respective increments.",
      "source": {
        "psi_id": "PSI-159",
        "doi": "10.60555/cyt1-kh64",
        "file": "documents/PSI-159/PSI-159_Reports_FinalRpt_ACME.CFI-G.pdf",
        "page": 38
      },
      "provenance": "Google Gemini (free tier)"
    },
    {
      "text": "Cool flame evidence was observed in certain tests, resulting in the identification of 15 cool flames.",
      "source": {
        "psi_id": "PSI-159",
        "doi": "10.60555/cyt1-kh64",
        "file": "documents/PSI-159/PSI-159_Reports_FinalRpt_ACME.CFI-G.pdf",
        "page": 38
      },
      "provenance": "Google Gemini (free tier)"
    },
    {
      "text": "The ACME CFI-G experimental table recorded 333 tests, comprising outcomes such as hot ignition leading to self-extinguishment in 175 tests, hot ignition with flow termination in 88 tests, and no hot ignition in 61 tests.",
      "source": {
